# Environment variables this app reads.
#
# As of Sprint 1 (app scaffold), the app does not read any user-supplied
# environment variables — it has no secrets, no database, and no external
# API calls yet (those land in later sprints: auth in Sprint 3, LLM
# integration in Sprint 4). The build identifier shown on the root page
# and returned by /api/health comes from VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, which
# Vercel sets automatically at build time — it is not something you set
# here.
#
# This file exists to establish the convention: every environment
# variable the app reads must be listed here with a placeholder value,
# and any variable exposed to client code must never hold a secret (see
# CLAUDE.md's Project standards section). When a later sprint adds a real
# variable, add it below as `NAME=placeholder-value` with a comment
# explaining what it's for and whether it's server-only or public.
